  "document": "B&K Precision 5491B 5-1/2 digit multimeter: the lab datasheet B_K_Precision_5491B_Digital_Multimeter__365_Days_.MDD (ATS-1042), cross-checked against the 2831E / 5491B User Manual",
  "pages": "User Manual v1.10.2024, Chapter 7 (5491B specifications), printed pp. 67 to 72; remote commands Chapters 5 and 6, pp. 41 to 64",
  "cite": "Lab datasheet ATS-1042 (365-day interval); manufacturer specification: B&K 5491B User Manual, Chapter 7, pp. 67 to 72",
  "limits": "Lab datasheet limits as the MDD prints them (default), or the manufacturer specification of the manual (the two differ only at the points listed in the point flags)",
  "report_note": "Limits are those of the lab datasheet ATS-1042 (365-day interval) unless the report header says the manufacturer specification was applied (B&K 5491B User Manual, Chapter 7, pp. 67 to 72). Each limit is nominal +/- (% of reading + % of range + resolution floor), as the datasheet prints it.",
  "note": "55 points: DC volts 5, AC volts 16, Frequency 4, Resistance 6, Continuity 1, DC current, 500 mA terminal 3, AC current, 500 mA terminal 11, DC current, 20 A terminal 3, AC current, 20 A terminal 6. Limits: the lab datasheet (default) or the manufacturer specification; they differ at 6 points (see the point details). The meter must be warmed up for half an hour; the specification is valid in the slow rate only (NPLC 10), which the program selects."
 },
